---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const GITHUB = 'https://github.com/hyphaehub/hyphaehub';
---

<Base title="Self-host HyphaeHub · Community Edition">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-substrate">Self-host the Community Edition</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink/70">
      Run the full HyphaeHub tracker on your own hardware. It is free and open-source, and your data stays
      in a local SQLite database and photos on a local volume. No account, no cloud, no limits.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-mycelium bg-substrate p-5 font-mono text-sm text-spore">
      <div class="text-mycelium/60"># clone and start with Docker Compose</div>
      <div class="mt-2">git clone {GITHUB}.git</div>
      <div>cd hyphaehub/infra</div>
      <div>docker compose up -d</div>
      <div class="mt-2 text-mycelium/60"># HyphaeHub is now at http://localhost:8080</div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-mycelium bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-substrate">What you get</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm text-ink/70">
          <li>• Full lifecycle tracker (source → jars → tubs → harvest)</li>
          <li>• Cost, yield, and biological-efficiency reporting</li>
          <li>• Built-in accounts (better-auth), no third-party service</li>
          <li>• SQLite database + local photo storage</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-mycelium bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-substrate">Requirements</h3>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm text-ink/70">
          <li>• Docker & Docker Compose</li>
          <li>• ~256 MB RAM</li>
          <li>• A folder for the database & photos</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-bold text-substrate">Cloud access to a self-hosted instance</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink/70">
      A paid cloud tier will let you securely reach your self-hosted instance from anywhere and
      from the mobile app, without exposing it to the public internet. This is on the roadmap.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <a
        href={GITHUB}
        class="rounded-xl bg-hyphae-600 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-spore hover:bg-hyphae-700"
      >
        View on GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
